# Toyota Yaris XP130 five-door hatchback, 2011-2020.
#
# The third-generation Yaris. UK launch August 2011, first customer deliveries
# September 2011, at £11,170 for the T2 three-door 1.0 VVT-i up to £15,385 for
# the T Spirit five-door 1.33 with MultiDrive S, on the road. Replaced in 2020
# by the XP210, which went on sale on 3 August 2020.
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Yaris-Gen3-Launch-Pack-2011.pdf
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/vehicles/yaris-2011-2020/
#
# Dimensions 3.885 x 1.695 x 1.500 m, wheelbase 2.510 m. Source: English
# Wikipedia, "Toyota Vitz", third-generation XP130 infobox: wheelbase
# 2,510 mm, length 3,885-3,930 mm for 2010-2016, width 1,695 mm, height
# 1,500 mm. The 3.885 m figure is the European pre-facelift car modelled. The
# corrected hull measures 3.89175 m, 6.75 mm over, 1.695 m wide, with the wheel
# centres 2.510 m apart (64.6 per cent of length). Mirrors extend to 1.824 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near-level side elevation and was the primary
# reference; image 2 the pre-facelift nose; image 3 the tail. Image 4 was
# excluded because it is a later facelift car with a different grille and
# bumper. The first pass failed the outline test — its roof curved down
# continuously into the tail — and one authorised correction round raised the
# roof line and made the hatch and tail panel more upright.
#
# Colours are Toyota GB names from the 2013 brochure, evidence grade (a):
# Cirrus White, Sintra Blue, Tyrol Silver, Chilli Red, Eclipse Black, Tidal
# Blue, Decuma Grey, Deep Aqua, Burning Red and Glacier Pearl. Four are
# modelled: Tyrol Silver, Cirrus White, Eclipse Black and Burning Red. Weights
# silver 3, white 3, red 2, black 2, total 10, provisional pending the central
# rebase.
#
# Speed 175 km/h, the hybrid and 1.33-litre cars' quoted maximum. Comfort
# 95/325, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 95. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: August 2011 intro, retires staggered 2023-2026 on a
# twelve- to fifteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-yaris-xp130.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-yaris-xp130.dae (64 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-yaris-xp130/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: after the correction round the side silhouette is close
# to the photograph but not identical — the rear glass is slightly less raked
# than the real car and the break between bonnet and front bumper is less
# distinct. The glazing lower edge is level, the flank crease understated and
# the tail lamps do not wrap as far round the corners as the photographs. The
# top view confirms a continuous painted roof. At 128 px the tall body, the
# high roof line and the upright hatch read as the XP130 and distinguish it
# from the rounder XP90.

obj=citycar
name=ToyotaYarisXP130(TyrolSilver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2011
intro_month=8
retire_year=2026
retire_month=6
speed=175
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=95
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=325

